id #uuid "d348807a-79ec-5100-8ae8-f8e91cc7a68e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x+y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132875/selection/63b0851837faa4f8ce3ed96b5c1711d36756408ac1cac57e125d710e455bcdd1" :answer/id #uuid "70000d0e-009f-58bc-bac3-c98a526d4055" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132875/selection/c703fde51d319de376ec3b5892e2f3b6384d7ccff49794523990161e7cd36ff1" :answer/id #uuid "74e8fe9e-962c-5c86-9e49-368d3d928e73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2xy}{\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})^{3}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132875/selection/79f46208ffaca0f356b1d4cb0d0a95d75cb64f1efc686763118b9fe5a6de7157" :answer/id #uuid "5dc6499a-fd7a-5c94-ab9b-86887fb1a414" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2xy}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132875/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "47854b94-911d-52f2-b21d-a72b251bac35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132875/selection/070693e704a124d3a51ca8432f4b751230679863f13213feb38bb7537c311a1c" :answer-field/choices ["q-132875/selection/070693e704a124d3a51ca8432f4b751230679863f13213feb38bb7537c311a1c" "q-132875/selection/e4c3a513c500c47288f32c313b7b17b8a6b650396a98568058ee451cc46c271b" "q-132875/selection/63b0851837faa4f8ce3ed96b5c1711d36756408ac1cac57e125d710e455bcdd1" "q-132875/selection/c703fde51d319de376ec3b5892e2f3b6384d7ccff49794523990161e7cd36ff1" "q-132875/selection/79f46208ffaca0f356b1d4cb0d0a95d75cb64f1efc686763118b9fe5a6de7157"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132875" :question/id #uuid "ded636a1-bfab-5a77-9994-1e43081f6a8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-132875" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{xx}(x,y)+{f}_{yy}(x,y)$ given that  ${f}_{x}(x,y)=x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}_{xx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find ${f}_{yy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y)+{f}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132875/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "503a0bfe-7c69-5ad0-ad1d-aa8692dae673"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132875"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80456/selection/4f6b4ffc8544741a40bc4a1333caf964ca2f7a5c6a1edd4b48482ccdd2583df4" :answer/id #uuid "e885de0a-db0c-5a22-a670-4ebecb2360c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4x}{{x}^{2}+y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80456/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "ac51f9f7-b74c-5fc6-a87e-c63c035449cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80456/selection/7e64b789e996730ac140252db755595fbfb770c9f96418ff8420837755fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "023b1a1a-ac2b-5f06-a506-ae2819c2add7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80456/selection/d1d2ebcbc04ea8135778dcd432142a832b23a69badf31575ab2c023070929d7a" :answer/id #uuid "b0eebbc0-c424-5a28-b715-b73c6cbc7127" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80456/selection/e21f1a0560baa15c0a7d5326e6703ccd2c36ab38f0322cb907ac85c903f3e645" :answer/id #uuid "3767127a-29b0-522d-83b6-f559b618e88d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2x+1}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80456/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a9694dc-d08c-5951-8037-cc6b95b10b98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80456/selection/d1d2ebcbc04ea8135778dcd432142a832b23a69badf31575ab2c023070929d7a" :answer-field/choices ["q-80456/selection/4f6b4ffc8544741a40bc4a1333caf964ca2f7a5c6a1edd4b48482ccdd2583df4" "q-80456/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-80456/selection/7e64b789e996730ac140252db755595fbfb770c9f96418ff8420837755fcd818" "q-80456/selection/d1d2ebcbc04ea8135778dcd432142a832b23a69badf31575ab2c023070929d7a" "q-80456/selection/e21f1a0560baa15c0a7d5326e6703ccd2c36ab38f0322cb907ac85c903f3e645"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80456" :question/id #uuid "e44348dd-af5f-5871-b215-119a4f001a40" :question/math-academy-id "q-80456" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{xy}(x,y)+{f}_{yx}(x,y)$ given that  ${f}_{x}(x,y)=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+y}$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}_{xy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+y}) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+y}) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find ${f}_{yx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+y}) \\\\  & =(-\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}})\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y)+{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =-\\frac{2x}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}-\\frac{2x}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4x}{({x}^{2}+y)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80456/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "503a0bfe-7c69-5ad0-ad1d-aa8692dae673"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80456"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80468/selection/a67526ab7a41e55eecd6c144a1fc2fa52cd013d542bf4f768ab1209cde63ab6e" :answer/id #uuid "595777da-9b6e-5590-a4e4-4e2e29b2a1b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80468/selection/0502a8c7457f41a56e60070d204bd20f17dc5befbd8c994c9e8b9ad8cc3bfaff" :answer/id #uuid "e5976a7d-c044-585f-b196-5d49790837b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80468/selection/bdfaa452f7de43ebd79f1dc0e55b759d85f2a0d5d58084eebfd24f2d3352bbae" :answer/id #uuid "b4b8d175-a9dd-58bb-8d2f-95e24742f3d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80468/selection/e7cb6b239664ae06a400ff3ce1e790520cd63651fa2322bdad85e9ab6976d1de" :answer/id #uuid "adc84c5b-85af-5cff-a902-8749759fcbaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80468/selection/2dcd8a1031779bdb21821719848e6365b706549b85f80eed283c263bd3ba16a8" :answer/id #uuid "ee01282a-e242-5b3f-9d68-e369ab91691b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80468/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e157cfed-9487-5ec6-bb5b-1b0b15476ba4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80468/selection/bdfaa452f7de43ebd79f1dc0e55b759d85f2a0d5d58084eebfd24f2d3352bbae" :answer-field/choices ["q-80468/selection/a67526ab7a41e55eecd6c144a1fc2fa52cd013d542bf4f768ab1209cde63ab6e" "q-80468/selection/0502a8c7457f41a56e60070d204bd20f17dc5befbd8c994c9e8b9ad8cc3bfaff" "q-80468/selection/bdfaa452f7de43ebd79f1dc0e55b759d85f2a0d5d58084eebfd24f2d3352bbae" "q-80468/selection/e7cb6b239664ae06a400ff3ce1e790520cd63651fa2322bdad85e9ab6976d1de" "q-80468/selection/2dcd8a1031779bdb21821719848e6365b706549b85f80eed283c263bd3ba16a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80468" :question/id #uuid "deab84e9-a867-5b1d-9a68-3b0761520810" :question/math-academy-id "q-80468" :question/problem "Find ${f}_{xy}(x,y)+{f}_{yx}(x,y)$ given that  ${f}_{x}(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${f}_{xy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\cdot (-2y)) \\\\  & =2xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find ${f}_{yx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-y\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =-y(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\cdot 2x) \\\\  & =2xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y)+{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =2xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})+2xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =4xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80468/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "503a0bfe-7c69-5ad0-ad1d-aa8692dae673"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80468"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132897/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "c8fce30e-4a9a-5f75-8bf2-f72339df3efe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132897/selection/9420bd993686febbc7bab9cad06140d93534fa634008fa5d1a005fe09b5d559c" :answer/id #uuid "225cef05-e4f3-5d19-8ccd-8d3fdc55eb09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132897/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "8bf0dc0b-4e2a-514b-8843-40f32a289210" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132897/selection/0aae0f62f78e37f51f0f104e1616f1edea4079865fd21fc152944066b39dedfe" :answer/id #uuid "91bd31df-5309-558f-a926-82da940f21b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132897/selection/fcc08b5493ae6f7b4bc0aad6b1791b974d36d4679ce4f932434b29e95cebea06" :answer/id #uuid "f7f7d2ab-d3b3-5f1a-866d-e571022d6c0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132897/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "13de9159-5c67-5f9d-a5c4-abc83e011769" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132897/selection/0aae0f62f78e37f51f0f104e1616f1edea4079865fd21fc152944066b39dedfe" :answer-field/choices ["q-132897/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-132897/selection/9420bd993686febbc7bab9cad06140d93534fa634008fa5d1a005fe09b5d559c" "q-132897/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-132897/selection/0aae0f62f78e37f51f0f104e1616f1edea4079865fd21fc152944066b39dedfe" "q-132897/selection/fcc08b5493ae6f7b4bc0aad6b1791b974d36d4679ce4f932434b29e95cebea06"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132897" :question/id #uuid "2e4c13f2-d7be-519c-b88f-355c27cc03a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-132897" :question/problem "Find ${g}_{xy}(x,y)+{g}_{yx}(x,y)$ at $(-1,2)$ given that ${g}_{x}(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x+2y}$ and ${g}_{y}(x,y)=\\frac{2}{x+2y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${g}_{xy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{1}{x+2y}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{(x+2y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo find ${g}_{yx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({g}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{2}{x+2y}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{(x+2y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we evaluate ${g}_{xy}(x,y)$ and ${g}_{yx}(x,y)$ at $(-1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xy}(-1,2) & =-\\frac{2}{((-1)+2(2))^{2}}=-\\frac{2}{9} \\\\ {g}_{yx}(-1,2) & =-\\frac{2}{((-1)+2(2))^{2}}=-\\frac{2}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n{g}_{xy}(-1,2)+{g}_{yx}(-1,2)=-\\frac{4}{9}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132897/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "503a0bfe-7c69-5ad0-ad1d-aa8692dae673"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132897"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132891/selection/8249ca98edbb0eefd6039a34b5df4c066383f0fdbe43d63631979e84e77a48dd" :answer/id #uuid "4a6e0624-85ff-5862-81e3-3518814477e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{e}^{-3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132891/selection/8e77b114af9c49ea6cd8744d18e5081850763025a320c982f38bbeb45705e1f6" :answer/id #uuid "05ae4dab-6217-5d45-9daa-124b3ebe7f6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({e}^{-1}-{e}^{-2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132891/selection/9e11fca0829731bcf7095fbe08d3f9c3c971cefec622b1eff73bc972ba625ef6" :answer/id #uuid "3a843fb8-ed5b-522b-ac6b-b89192d4aba6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132891/selection/a3dc28ec40c3651faf01e6e29e3bfd246efcd97762f36f1a8406c13fbb1f21d0" :answer/id #uuid "c58704fe-6aee-5ea6-b85e-e0dd2e1a3a6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{e}^{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132891/selection/4fbda233d26f6145300f008f711a7bf710c398022d3f5b7b40d1811e9c0d08d2" :answer/id #uuid "f976fb1a-8e05-5b3b-afe8-98786eb10a67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{e}^{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132891/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "096ebacf-d3a4-57e5-9588-292760252d78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132891/selection/4fbda233d26f6145300f008f711a7bf710c398022d3f5b7b40d1811e9c0d08d2" :answer-field/choices ["q-132891/selection/8249ca98edbb0eefd6039a34b5df4c066383f0fdbe43d63631979e84e77a48dd" "q-132891/selection/8e77b114af9c49ea6cd8744d18e5081850763025a320c982f38bbeb45705e1f6" "q-132891/selection/9e11fca0829731bcf7095fbe08d3f9c3c971cefec622b1eff73bc972ba625ef6" "q-132891/selection/a3dc28ec40c3651faf01e6e29e3bfd246efcd97762f36f1a8406c13fbb1f21d0" "q-132891/selection/4fbda233d26f6145300f008f711a7bf710c398022d3f5b7b40d1811e9c0d08d2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132891" :question/id #uuid "7cc4a771-b441-5088-905e-971d433b9763" :question/math-academy-id "q-132891" :question/problem "Find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)\\cdot {g}_{yy}(x,y)$ at $(0,1)$ given that ${g}_{x}(x,y)=2{e}^{2x-y}$ and ${g}_{y}(x,y)=-{e}^{2x-y}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({g}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{e}^{2x-y}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{2x-y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo find ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${g}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{yy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({g}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{e}^{2x-y}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2x-y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we evaluate ${g}_{xx}(x,y)$ and ${g}_{yy}(x,y)$ at $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xx}(0,1) & =4{e}^{2(0)-1}=4{e}^{-1} \\\\ {g}_{yy}(0,1) & ={e}^{2(0)-1}={e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n{g}_{xx}(0,1)\\cdot {g}_{yy}(0,1)=4{e}^{-1}\\cdot {e}^{-1}=4{e}^{-2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132891/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "503a0bfe-7c69-5ad0-ad1d-aa8692dae673"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132891"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65068/selection/c9a65ecf0d11e33071e92b278c15c9b564e22dc15a38f2fb20362060a86d8654" :answer/id #uuid "8eb74cbd-5f37-556f-b5a7-7d97e60fd7b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1+xy){e}^{xy}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65068/selection/251e43bd408e42a657dc7a6a5011c69ff68df40a6ad26e80b27d2ad8dc4fb7ad" :answer/id #uuid "4a062bc7-1894-5292-9679-b8f8c2b076db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2(1+xy){e}^{xy}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65068/selection/f2aa53fc3784582c99a5ef11eb6e28e4452f83e65b97a04c0c6e46743fb26779" :answer/id #uuid "c1d65a62-afa0-5619-8421-b4ea789a417f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(2-xy){e}^{xy}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65068/selection/e5bdae6c0e2f3772b75511f04602067d42bfe8a3aad6e368ff0257ad596ef4e5" :answer/id #uuid "13fa376c-22fa-5bbb-b6ea-2d61be4675f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(2+xy){e}^{xy}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65068/selection/456c436169d43b15a970a8576edb383d783dc4e1dcdbfe98f5658204918cea9f" :answer/id #uuid "3fe95d8d-64e7-5e26-8497-4ba50d04a5a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2-xy){e}^{xy}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65068/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "29c9042e-e21e-5fb9-812e-4399723e1296" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-65068/selection/e5bdae6c0e2f3772b75511f04602067d42bfe8a3aad6e368ff0257ad596ef4e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-65068/selection/c9a65ecf0d11e33071e92b278c15c9b564e22dc15a38f2fb20362060a86d8654" "q-65068/selection/251e43bd408e42a657dc7a6a5011c69ff68df40a6ad26e80b27d2ad8dc4fb7ad" "q-65068/selection/f2aa53fc3784582c99a5ef11eb6e28e4452f83e65b97a04c0c6e46743fb26779" "q-65068/selection/e5bdae6c0e2f3772b75511f04602067d42bfe8a3aad6e368ff0257ad596ef4e5" "q-65068/selection/456c436169d43b15a970a8576edb383d783dc4e1dcdbfe98f5658204918cea9f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65068" :question/id #uuid "496a6dc2-a2be-5cc0-b846-7ba6991e3da0" :question/math-academy-id "q-65068" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}_{xxy}(x,y)$ given that $f(x,y)={e}^{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{xy}) \\\\  & =y{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{xx}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y{e}^{xy}) \\\\  & =y(y{e}^{xy}) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}{e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find ${f}_{xxy}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{xx}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xxy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{xx}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}{e}^{xy}) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot {e}^{xy}+{y}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{xy}\\cdot x \\\\  & =y(2+xy){e}^{xy}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-65068/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83724b66-0f15-5b94-9576-76e9dfd56d38"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65068"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36019"] :question/problem "Evaluate ${f}_{xyz}(1,1,1)$ for $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{yz}{x-2z}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{yz}{x-2z}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{yz}{(x-2z)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{xy}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{x}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\frac{yz}{(x-2z)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{z}{(x-2z)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{xy}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({f}_{xy}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-\\frac{z}{(x-2z)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1\\cdot (x-2z)^{2}-z\\cdot 2(x-2z)\\cdot (-2)}{(x-2z)^{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(x-2z)^{2}+4z(x-2z)}{(x-2z)^{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{x-2z+4z}{(x-2z)^{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{x+2z}{(x-2z)^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate ${f}_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ at $(1,1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(1,1,1) & =-\\frac{1+2\\cdot 1}{(1-2\\cdot 1)^{3}}=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-132940/selection/b336641abcb999c21c9e53c96c83b284fdf2bf3a3de0d87fa53f648928975e27" :answer/id #uuid "0561a2a8-2fcc-5572-96ff-df92d77932e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132940/selection/351e49f2f674aafda3c76e38d802ba7403f7c112fef9478c9adc8c26b573e827" :answer/id #uuid "93687c3f-4873-5a2e-bd80-c36784b98df2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{25}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132940/selection/2aef90071200a7bc65baa2d03f49803233ca7b2dc16865265136281ee914878b" :answer/id #uuid "44d51cea-5855-59b3-8e90-e9b235ab1fba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132940/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer/id #uuid "68964bce-db0f-53b4-a514-d148f52dabff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132940/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "7720eac2-7227-5274-b30e-099a6955fafa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132940/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6dd68d30-096e-5201-8a7e-a7cef951571b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132940/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer-field/choices ["q-132940/selection/b336641abcb999c21c9e53c96c83b284fdf2bf3a3de0d87fa53f648928975e27" "q-132940/selection/351e49f2f674aafda3c76e38d802ba7403f7c112fef9478c9adc8c26b573e827" "q-132940/selection/2aef90071200a7bc65baa2d03f49803233ca7b2dc16865265136281ee914878b" "q-132940/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" "q-132940/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132940" :question/id #uuid "a0c6f830-201a-5907-abfd-ac0c89aa4495" :question/math-academy-id "q-132940" :question/problem "Evaluate ${f}_{xyz}(-5,2,3)$ for $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+z).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+z)) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{xy}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{x}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+z)) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot \\frac{1}{y+z} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{y+z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{xy}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({f}_{xy}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{2x}{y+z}) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{1}{y+z}) \\\\  & =2x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{(y+z)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{(y+z)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate ${f}_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ at $(-5,2,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyz}(-5,2,3) & =-\\frac{2(-5)}{(2+3)^{2}}=\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132940/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83724b66-0f15-5b94-9576-76e9dfd56d38"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132940"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132961/selection/63079cc748dc757e7a8e5256fd2c9d955e6cf36193b2548b0f6e7b6b72fbf55c" :answer/id #uuid "7461a1c5-a4a9-58d3-8fcc-314f7414a508" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132961/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "a365acee-007d-5f2e-9fcf-19854a1794da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132961/selection/8edf36f0d0c04b8e0e3f881a66fab0f1901a06368d5ca1f6d437f77714de6bc5" :answer/id #uuid "9c71b7fc-f26d-5a5a-9647-6482d9d39b4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132961/selection/a3f72a33bd97dbcb26e67e320a072cf6fd98f5dc94f2de44db2fa04c176254bd" :answer/id #uuid "8c0550b4-7dac-592a-b59a-94f534d4d874" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132961/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "af4a9766-e350-5511-822f-4f0f6c812d74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132961/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "742611f3-c4c7-542b-9c90-2a48a56ed775" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132961/selection/8edf36f0d0c04b8e0e3f881a66fab0f1901a06368d5ca1f6d437f77714de6bc5" :answer-field/choices ["q-132961/selection/63079cc748dc757e7a8e5256fd2c9d955e6cf36193b2548b0f6e7b6b72fbf55c" "q-132961/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-132961/selection/8edf36f0d0c04b8e0e3f881a66fab0f1901a06368d5ca1f6d437f77714de6bc5" "q-132961/selection/a3f72a33bd97dbcb26e67e320a072cf6fd98f5dc94f2de44db2fa04c176254bd" "q-132961/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132961" :question/id #uuid "ee9df1f5-cb1d-59c5-8894-54201c221d7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-132961" :question/problem "Evaluate ${f}_{xxz}(1,\\frac{1}{2},\\pi )$ for $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡xyz) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)\\cdot yz \\\\  & =yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{xx}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{x}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xx}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{x}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(yz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =yz\\cdot (-yz\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{xxz}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating ${f}_{xx}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xxz}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({f}_{xx}(x,y,z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(-{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}\\frac{∂}{∂z}({z}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}\\cdot (2z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)+xy{z}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =-{y}^{2}z(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xyz)+xyz\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xyz))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate ${f}_{xxz}(x,y,z)$ at $(1,\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xxz}(1,\\frac{1}{2},\\pi ) & =-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot (2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi )+1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132961/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83724b66-0f15-5b94-9576-76e9dfd56d38"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132961"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-65071/selection/d62e60da9707e87b596bc06dcffa099ab54d954b6316b33ecd3f5565a61f07f2" :answer/id #uuid "cfe517db-b499-5ef7-9194-f08d147ac28a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2y}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65071/selection/e578e655e7beeb0cbb3c52c7180032437bcbd46b4c8906973c3e06b8aa9ab569" :answer/id #uuid "9b008f21-7439-5aee-ac6e-59588a0a877f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4y}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65071/selection/a167ab3b8d2758ce109c047ac3f5d435aa4646d31c1701226ef977a1d37af78c" :answer/id #uuid "b7eb1695-cfb1-51d5-9b77-e9e9b7ecaebb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65071/selection/b434fa149e3beb238ff6a7302233a38f95ce6bfb3689a16a352a85571f4f252f" :answer/id #uuid "75572fda-0dd9-5031-a2ea-eb17ac3dd1ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4+y}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65071/selection/f00dfe5f5af04310962dd91c5be13353115e7d95a977b24440a5ed3e54255a56" :answer/id #uuid "1f5d3bfd-9923-5575-a61d-6c027a071ca7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y}{4x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-65071/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0baa3a37-991b-59f6-9209-b96a40755564" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-65071/selection/e578e655e7beeb0cbb3c52c7180032437bcbd46b4c8906973c3e06b8aa9ab569" :answer-field/choices ["q-65071/selection/d62e60da9707e87b596bc06dcffa099ab54d954b6316b33ecd3f5565a61f07f2" "q-65071/selection/e578e655e7beeb0cbb3c52c7180032437bcbd46b4c8906973c3e06b8aa9ab569" "q-65071/selection/a167ab3b8d2758ce109c047ac3f5d435aa4646d31c1701226ef977a1d37af78c" "q-65071/selection/b434fa149e3beb238ff6a7302233a38f95ce6bfb3689a16a352a85571f4f252f" "q-65071/selection/f00dfe5f5af04310962dd91c5be13353115e7d95a977b24440a5ed3e54255a56"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65071" :question/id #uuid "e606e43e-b267-5b19-ab3d-7c9894aaf615" :question/math-academy-id "q-65071" :question/problem "Calculate ${f}_{yxx}(x,y)$ given that $f(x,y)={y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{yx}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4y}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find ${f}_{yxx}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{yx}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yxx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{yx}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{4y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot x-4y\\cdot 1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4y}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-65071/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83724b66-0f15-5b94-9576-76e9dfd56d38"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65071"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3127"] :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac {\\partial^2 f }{\\partial x\\partial y}$ given that $\\dfrac {\\partial f}{\\partial y} =  \\dfrac {2y} {x + y^2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\dfrac {\\partial^2 f }{\\partial x\\partial y},$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\dfrac {\\partial f}{\\partial y}$ with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂x∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂f}{∂y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{2y}{x+{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =2y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({(x+{y}^{2})}^{-1}) \\\\  & =-2y(x+{y}^{2})^{-2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2y}{{(x+{y}^{2})}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3129"] :question/problem "Find $f_{xy}(x,y)+f_{yx}(x,y)$ given that  $f_x(x,y)=y\\cos(xy)$ and $f_y(x,y)=x\\cos(xy).$" :question/worked-solution "To find $f_{xy}(x,y),$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $f_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+y(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSimilarly, to find $f_{yx}(x,y),$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $f_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+x(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y)+{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy) \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-3130"] :question/problem "Evaluate $g_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ at $(1,2,3)$ if $g_x(x,y,z) = 2x y z +  y^3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $g_{xy}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating $g_{x}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xy}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xyz+{y}^{3}) \\\\  & =2xz+3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find $g_{xyz}(x,y,z)$ by differentiating $g_{xy}(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xyz}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2xz+3{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{xyz}(1,2,3) & =2(1) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
